      "obligation": "refuter:27:1",
      "id": "def-rpm-spacetime-observer-and-worldline",
      "location": "Definition, massive worldline, sentence 2",
      "defect": "false-claim",
      "evidence": "The item says a C² curve “is the smooth subclass” of [[def-gr-timelike-worldline-and-proper-time]]. That supplier distinguishes finite Cᵏ regularity from the smooth (C∞) case. In a flat inertial chart, x⁰=ct, x¹=ε|t|^(5/2), x²=x³=0 on a sufficiently small interval is future timelike and C² but not C³. Thus the stated C² class is not a subclass of smooth worldlines.",
      "severity": "fatal",
      "subject_type": "in-run-dependency",
      "consumer_id": "def-rpm-body-moments",
      "observed_source": {
